templates.body:
Draft an internal case memo from these notes. Structure it as Facts, Issues, Rules, Analysis, Conclusion. Do not invent authorities: where a rule needs a citation, write [citation needed] instead. Flag any assumption you had to make.

Matter: {{matter}}
Jurisdiction: {{jurisdiction}}
Client position: {{client_position}}

Notes:
{{notes}}

Summarise the following contract for a busy partner: parties and roles, term and termination, payment, key obligations of each side, liability and indemnity, IP, confidentiality, governing law, and any clause that is unusual or one-sided. Quote the exact wording for anything you flag as a risk. End with five questions to raise with the client.

Client: {{client_name}}
Our side: {{our_side}}

Contract text:
{{contract_text}}

Draft a demand letter on behalf of {{client_name}} to {{recipient}}. Tone: formal and firm, no threats beyond what the facts support. State the facts, the obligation breached, the remedy demanded ({{remedy}}), a deadline of {{deadline}}, and what follows if it passes. Leave placeholders for any figure or date I did not give you.

Facts:
{{facts}}

Write a short client update email to {{client_name}} about {{matter}}. Plain language, no jargon, three parts: where things stand, what happens next and when, what I need from them. Do not give legal conclusions I have not stated below.

Status and next steps:
{{status}}
